1
00:00:00,590 --> 00:00:02,870
OK, everybody.

2
00:00:02,870 --> 00:00:06,320
I want to welcome Harry and his daughter Michelle

3
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:07,860
to Thanksgiving with us.

4
00:00:07,860 --> 00:00:09,020
Thank you, Dr. Stewart.

5
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:09,820
Call me Philip.

6
00:00:09,820 --> 00:00:10,840
OK.

7
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:13,200
But first, I think we should take a moment

8
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:15,770
and remember the meaning of Thanksgiving.

9
00:00:15,770 --> 00:00:18,440
Philip, I took Michelle to a school play

10
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:19,980
about the first Thanksgiving.

11
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:22,500
Well, why don't you tell us about that, Michelle?

12
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:24,570
Thanksgiving was about the Pilgrims,

13
00:00:24,570 --> 00:00:26,240
the first settlers in America.

14
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:28,560
They shared the first harvest with the Indians

15
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:30,480
and gave thanks.

16
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:31,470
All right.

17
00:00:31,470 --> 00:00:34,950
Then in that spirit let each of us give thanks.

18
00:00:34,950 --> 00:00:36,860
Each in his own way.

19
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:38,250
Who wants to begin?

20
00:00:38,250 --> 00:00:40,560
I will.

21
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:45,190
I give thanks for being here with my family and for being well,

22
00:00:45,190 --> 00:00:46,690
so I can enjoy you all.

23
00:00:46,690 --> 00:00:48,110
All rihgt!

24
00:00:48,110 --> 00:00:51,060
We love you, Grandpa.

25
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:57,470
I'd like to give thanks for a healthy year, a good job,

26
00:00:57,470 --> 00:01:00,500
and for meeting Harry and Michelle.

27
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:02,890
We'd like to give thanks for meeting Susan

28
00:01:02,890 --> 00:01:04,150
and the Stewart family.

29
00:01:04,150 --> 00:01:06,490
I love you, Daddy.

30
00:01:06,490 --> 00:01:07,300
Thanks, Harry.

31
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:08,830
That was very kind of you.

32
00:01:08,830 --> 00:01:12,480
I'd like to give thanks for Grandpa coming to live with us.

33
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:14,900
And I'd also like to thank my math teacher

34
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:17,670
for giving me a passing grade.

35
00:01:17,670 --> 00:01:21,380
And call me, Alexandra.

36
00:01:21,380 --> 00:01:22,240
Oh, Robbie!

37
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:24,210
She'll call.

38
00:01:24,210 --> 00:01:26,020
You go first, Marilyn.

39
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:26,830
I'm thinking.

40
00:01:26,830 --> 00:01:28,790
You go first.

41
00:01:28,790 --> 00:01:34,860
Well, you all know I'm working on my photo album.

42
00:01:34,860 --> 00:01:36,420
It's not finished yet.

43
00:01:36,420 --> 00:01:40,480
And I'd like to thank Marilyn for being so patient.

44
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:42,130
Thanks, Richard.

45
00:01:42,130 --> 00:01:44,240
I should thank you for encouraging me

46
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:46,240
to keep working on my fashion designs.

47
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:51,200
I'm lucky to have a husband with an artistic eye.

48
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:56,090
Oh, we have a lot to be thankful for.

49
00:01:56,090 --> 00:01:57,990
For the food on this table.

50
00:01:57,990 --> 00:01:59,740
Just like the Pilgrims.

51
00:01:59,740 --> 00:02:01,830
I'll go along with that, Ellen.

52
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:07,520
Well, help me serve, Robbie.

53
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:09,190
It was a wonderful meal, Mrs. Stewart.

54
00:02:09,190 --> 00:02:09,990
Thank you.

55
00:02:09,990 --> 00:02:11,910
And now to see the end of the football game.

56
00:02:11,910 --> 00:02:13,760
Exactly.

57
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:15,400
Where are you going, Philip?

58
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:17,310
Remember, the Michigan football game?

59
00:02:17,310 --> 00:02:20,150
And Michigan needs a touchdown.

60
00:02:20,150 --> 00:02:21,630
Did you forget something?

61
00:02:21,630 --> 00:02:24,560
Dad, your famous apple pie.

62
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:26,900
Just let me see the score, Ellen.

63
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:27,990
Go ahead, Philip.

64
00:02:27,990 --> 00:02:40,930
We should all take a little break before dessert.

65
00:02:40,930 --> 00:02:44,570
Oh, who could that be?

66
00:02:44,570 --> 00:02:46,920
Oh, it must be Alexandra.

67
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:49,050
I invited her to come by for dessert.

68
00:02:49,050 --> 00:02:50,240
You did?

69
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:51,520
I like Ellen.

70
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:53,030
You know everyone, Alexandra.

71
00:02:53,030 --> 00:02:56,510
No, she doesn't know Harry Bennett and his daughter Michelle.

72
00:02:56,510 --> 00:02:57,460
Nice to meet you.

73
00:02:57,460 --> 00:02:58,630
Hi.

74
00:02:58,630 --> 00:03:00,270
Hello, Alexandra.

75
00:03:00,270 --> 00:03:01,100
Hi, Marilyn.

76
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:01,770
Hi, Susan.

77
00:03:01,770 --> 00:03:03,050
Happy Thanksgiving.

78
00:03:03,050 --> 00:03:05,670
And Alexandra brought us a pumpkin pie.

79
00:03:05,670 --> 00:03:08,270
Please sit down, Alexandra.

80
00:03:08,270 --> 00:03:12,660
Dad, Richard--Alexandra's here.

81
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:13,880
Michigan needs a touchdown.

82
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:15,070
Three minutes to play.

83
00:03:15,070 --> 00:03:16,700
Hi, Alexandra. Welcome.

84
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:17,890
Hello, Alexandra.

85
00:03:17,890 --> 00:03:19,730
Yes, Michigan needs a touchdown.

86
00:03:19,730 --> 00:03:22,920
One tiny little touchdown, with just three minutes to play.

87
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:24,720
You want Michigan to win.

88
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:25,780
How'd you guess?

89
00:03:25,780 --> 00:03:40,860
And Alexandra brought us a pumpkin pie.

90
00:03:40,860 --> 00:03:42,530
What happened?

91
00:03:42,530 --> 00:03:45,450
We forgot to turn the oven on.

92
00:03:45,450 --> 00:03:48,480
We did?

93
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:50,350
Philip, why don't you go

94
00:03:50,350 --> 00:03:52,460
watch the last three minutes of the game.

95
00:03:52,460 --> 00:03:55,580
I will serve coffee and pumpkin pie.

96
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:59,180
OK. I'll be back in a few minutes.

97
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:01,830
Robbie, would you bring the dessert plates.

98
00:04:01,830 --> 00:04:04,020
And, Marilyn, would you pour coffee, please.

99
00:04:04,020 --> 00:04:08,340
Sure, Ellen.

100
00:04:08,340 --> 00:04:10,810
How was your Thanksgiving dinner, Alexandra?

101
00:04:10,810 --> 00:04:12,770
Just wonderful, Mr. Stewart.

102
00:04:12,770 --> 00:04:14,620
The Molinas are a large family.

103
00:04:14,620 --> 00:04:16,490
I love being with them.

104
00:04:16,490 --> 00:04:18,120
I'm glad you came by, Alexandra.

105
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:23,400
I am, too.

106
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:28,190
Touchdown! Touchdown! Touchdown!

107
00:04:28,190 --> 00:04:29,990
Great Thanksgiving.

108
00:04:29,990 --> 00:04:32,410
Lots to be thankful for.

109
00:04:32,410 --> 00:04:34,830
Michigan scored a touchdown.

110
00:04:34,830 --> 00:04:37,070
Alexandra came by.

111
00:04:37,070 --> 00:04:41,510
And nobody misses Philip's famous apple pie.

112
00:04:41,510 --> 00:04:44,510
Oh, Grandpa!
